{title: We Rise Up}
{subtitle: Psalms 20:7–8}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
May He remember all your [F/A]offerings
Re[Gm]ceive your burnt offering [Eb]with favor
[Bb]Give you what your heart de[F]sires
Bring all [Eb]your plans to pass
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
We shout for [Bb]joy at your [F/A]victory
Raise [Gm]our banners in the name of [Eb]our God
The [Bb]LORD fulfills every re[F]quest
Your plans in [Eb]His hands are held
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Now I know [Bb]the LORD saves his a[F]nointed
[Gm]He answers from his ho[Eb]ly heaven
With the [Bb]saving power of his [F]right hand
We call [Gm]on the name [F]of the [Eb]LORD our God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Some [Bb]trust in chariots [F]and some in hors[Gm]es
But we call on the name [Eb]of the LORD
[Bb]They are brought to their [F]knees and fall
But we [Eb]rise up and stand firm
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Now I [Bb]know the LORD saves his [F]anointed
[Gm]He answers from his ho[Eb]ly heaven
With the [Bb]saving power of his [F]right hand
We call on [Gm]the name of [F]the LORD our [Eb]God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
They [Bb]fall, but we [F]rise up
Standing [Gm]firm in the name of the [Eb]LORD [Bb]
{end_of_verse}
